Server network ownership

Installation always uses the physical Ethernet adapter. The shared uplink
stage binds its MAC and the optional Wi-Fi adapter to the profile's stable
names. NetworkManager owns the installed server's physical connections;
unrelated ifupdown stanzas remain unmanaged. Role services use the selected
default route and the firewall permits only the declared physical pair.

MANAGED_NETWORK_PRIMARY_IFACE selects metric 100; the fallback uses 600.
WIFI_ENABLE controls private AP preconfiguration from the initrd-root
/preseed.env restricted reader. A saved AP may reconnect automatically even
when that flag was false at installation. Its IPv4 and enabled IPv6 addresses
are the Ethernet installation address plus one in the same prefix. Reserve
that pair outside a dynamic DHCP allocation pool. A changed Ethernet lease
requires explicit paired-address policy maintenance; arbitrary changing DHCP
leases are not qualified by the fresh-install static evidence.

IPV6_ENABLE=false disables IPv6 on both physical uplinks, not loopback or
unrelated private job namespaces. Desktop veth/proxy/session configuration is
not staged for server roles. Technitium management stays loopback-only and
port 53 stays closed until explicit private configuration.
